WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.120
Spider-Man: No Way Home might just have served up&nbsp;
one of the most emotionally devastating endings in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.920
the Marvel Cinematic Universe to date. And this&nbsp;
is coming from the franchise that gave us this.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.480
"I don't know what's happening, I don't know-"

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.080
"I don't wanna go, sir, please, I&nbsp;
don't wanna go. I don't wanna go."

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.480
No Way Home concludes with the multiverse&nbsp;
breaking apart, forcing Doctor Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.960
to do everything in his power to stop it from&nbsp;
crumbling. After cosmic cracks form in the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.280
silhouettes of various characters appear,&nbsp;
each ready to enter the MCU dimension.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.360
It's at this point that Peter Parker realizes that&nbsp;
they can prevent the multiverse from breaking by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.000
having Strange make the world forget who Peter&nbsp;
Parker is — including those he loves most.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.320
Considering the hefty emotional weight to this&nbsp;
whole scene, you might be forgiven for having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.080
missed some of the characters who appeared&nbsp;
within those interdimensional doorways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.800
They're kinda hard to make out,&nbsp;
and they don't appear for long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.800
but if you look closely enough, you may&nbsp;
be able to catch a few surprising cameos.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.040
Right now, there's been no official confirmation&nbsp;
about who exactly appears in the cracks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.880
At first glance, they may even appear as&nbsp;
intentionally distorted images designed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.680
give the impression that they could be pretty much&nbsp;
anyone. However, for the keen comic book observer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.280
some of those silhouettes definitely&nbsp;
seem more recognizable than others.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.160
The figure most likely to stand out in fans' minds&nbsp;
is that of Rhino, bearing a striking resemblance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.240
to the comic book iteration of the character —&nbsp;
as opposed to Paul Giamatti's more mechanical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.400
version from The Amazing Spider-Man 2. This,&nbsp;
of course, seems to suggest that the tear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.640
reality would have brought in many more variants&nbsp;
on Spider-Man villains than those fans know from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.360
previous movies. And it seems like we might have&nbsp;
seen a few who haven't appeared on-screen at all.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.000
Since seeing No Way Home, MCU fans and audiences&nbsp;
have suggested that some of the other villains on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.560
display in the final showdown include Scorpion and&nbsp;
Kraven the Hunter. While these foes haven't suited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.200
up on screen just yet, there have been teases to&nbsp;
suggest they could enter the live-action sphere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.520
Kraven, aka Sergei Kravinoff, is one of&nbsp;
the more obvious figures in No Way Home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.440
thanks to the spear the silhouette appears to&nbsp;
be holding. You can also make out some thickness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.840
around the silhouette's shoulders and head, which&nbsp;
could be the mane of his signature lion's pelt.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.240
The scorpion figure is a little more challenging&nbsp;
to make out, but it's easier to see once you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.200
know it's there. This villain appears to be bent&nbsp;
over, with a tail that curves up just behind him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.600
In this appearance, it looks like Scorpion is&nbsp;
crawling as opposed to standing up, suggesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.680
that this is a slightly different version from&nbsp;
that which appears in the main comic books.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.520
It's probably a good time for Marvel to&nbsp;
be referencing these particular villains.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.280
Kraven is getting his own Sony-produced&nbsp;
movie in the near future, while Scorpion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.440
was hinted at in Spider-Man: Homecoming.&nbsp;
In that movie, Mac Gargan appears as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.080
potential buyer for the Vulture's weapons. He&nbsp;
subsequently appears in the post-credits scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.920
for the movie, in which he attempts to learn&nbsp;
Spider-Man's real identity through Vulture.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.600
"I got some boys on the&nbsp;
outside who'd love to meet him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.120
You know, take a picture, slice his&nbsp;
throat, put his head in the dryer…"

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.920
Seeing how No Way Home's ending has set up a&nbsp;
whole new era for the MCU's Spider-Man, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.400
entirely within the realm of reason that Scorpion&nbsp;
might appear as a proper villain in the future.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.920
While Kraven, Scorpion, and Rhino have been&nbsp;
the three most discussed villains from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.560
crackling sky scene, a few other famous comic book&nbsp;
characters are thought to have been spotted, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.840
One of them is Black Cat — whose appearance&nbsp;
shouldn't come as much of a surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.320
since Spider-Man producer Amy Pascal has suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.360
that the infamous thief is bound&nbsp;
for the big screen in the future.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.040
There have also been some other obscure&nbsp;
guesses about who is hiding in the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.040
with some fans claiming to have seen Madame&nbsp;
Web, while others believe to have spotted the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.760
multiverse-hopping vampire known as Morlun.&nbsp;
And who knows who else might yet be found?

